'' See the source's header. A fixed-length narrow string reaching a 'byref as string'
'' constructor parameter is CONVERTED into a descriptor of its own, not passed as its
'' own characters.
''
'' The assertion is on fb_StrAssign building the temporary, because the call takes a
'' pointer either way and reads right in the broken IR too. Measured: the broken
'' compiler emitted 'call void _ZN1UC1ER8FBSTRINGj(%3, @@gz, %4)' -- the char array
'' handed straight to the FBSTRING* parameter.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/ctor-conv-fixed-string-arg.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-NOT: _ZN1UC1ER8FBSTRINGj(%3, @@gz
